 "reports_individuals_with_tnfaip3_variant": true,
 "relevance_note": "Single-patient case report of a woman with a working diagnosis of arterial tortuosity syndrome: 'the patient was heterozygous in the SLC2A10 gene for a sequence variant defined as c.394 C>T'.",
 "method_note": "Read by hand; no tables. One in-scope person (single unnamed case-report patient, label 'patient'). The 'at least 4 individuals' previously reported as compound heterozygous for c.394 C>T (refs 3,4) are described only as a count, so they get no rows. Only one SLC2A10 variant was detected; the authors say a second variant may have been missed and deletion/duplication testing was not done; diagnosis is called a 'working diagnosis'. Variant type 'missense' taken from the authors' wording 'predicted to result in the amino acid substitution p.Arg132Trp' (the word missense is not printed). Genomic coordinate 20-45354069-C-T comes from reference [2] (gnomAD v2.1.1 entry) cited for this variant; no genome build printed. Pathogenicity left not reported: the paper implies but does not state a classification for c.394 C>T ('the second pathogenic variant'). Age 37 years is age at referral, recorded as last evaluation; no age at diagnosis or onset. Vital status not stated explicitly (discharged well on postoperative day 5). Paper misspells the gene once as 'SLCA2A10'. Positive ANA/cardiolipin/SSA serology recorded as observed features. No contradictions found.",
